 ~#resolved(glob_engine): "Which matcher backs the shared resolver: node fs.glob (absent on the engines floor ^20.19), a declared picomatch dependency (it sits in node_modules today but no package.json declares it), or a small in-house ** and * matcher limited to what prompts/** and **/*.spw need? — picomatch, declared as a dependency of packages/spw-cli (^4.0.7; it was only present transitively through vitest); evidence: user decision 2026-10-12, declared in packages/spw-cli/package.json, cli tests 265 of 265 pass"
 ~#resolved(walker_fork): "fs-walk.ts has the shared collectSpwFiles, yet geometry, format, authority, mass, pulse and ls/scan each keep a private copy; does the resolver replace all of them in one commit, or only the sense verbs (census, graph, query) first? — first the three sense verbs (census, graph, query); the other private walkers follow once the resolver is proven; evidence: user decision 2026-10-12"
 ~#observed(glob_gap): "2026-10-12 repro, run by the rescoping agent: spw census 'prompts/**' reported files 0, spw graph 'prompts/**' files 0, spw query --from 'prompts/**' scanned=0, while spw census prompts reported files 95 lines 9205; evidence: no glob handling in fs-walk.ts, and SelectionIR in packages/spw-seed/src/ir/slices.ts is a type only"
 ~#resolved(census_vs_roster): "census (population) vs roster (list) — census is the canonical verb, invent/inventory/inv are aliases in commands.ts; evidence: stream 2026-10-12 14:26"
 ~#resolved(graph_rename): "dual-primary map+graph one release then prefer graph? — graph is canonical and map/topo are aliases; evidence: stream 2026-10-12 14:26"
 ~#resolved(surface_vs_stack): "surface composite primary; stack thin? — stack is the canonical command and surface/profile are its aliases; evidence: stream 2026-10-12 14:26"
 ~#resolved(profile_compat): "profile -> surface stack vs profile -> full surface? — profile resolves to the stack command; evidence: stream 2026-10-12 14:26"
 ~#resolved(surface_p0): "implement surface as HotSession.inspect wrapper first? — moot, surface shipped as an alias of stack; evidence: stream 2026-10-12 14:26"
 ~#resolved(ultra_short): "ship any of inv/geom/topo only, or also g for graph? — inv, geom, topo aliases exist and no g alias; evidence: stream 2026-10-12 14:26"
}
